<title>GREECE: BANK/GREECE SELLS 370MLN ECUS AT FIX, ECU FIRMS.</title>
<headline>BANK/GREECE SELLS 370MLN ECUS AT FIX, ECU FIRMS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Greece sold 370 million ecus to banks at Tuesday's fixing and ecu/drachma landed higher at 301.20 from Friday's 300.85 drachmas.</p>
<p>A dealer said that Salomon Brothers was mainly behind the ecu purchases.</p>
<p>Small amounts of $25 millon and 75 million marks were also sold by the central bank at the fixing, a dealer at a state bank said.</p>
<p>&quot;Interbank liquidity depends on forex inflows and these outflows drain funds and might turn the market short,&quot; a dealer at a state bank said.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
